{"signature": "7b510b01861c3d51909cbdd92301ce4c8645cdb0ff335c6b318f02125e6f813e", "result": {"checks": {"check": {"scope": {"id": "check", "service": "gdocs", "file": "data.json", "pointer": "/docs_documents", "field": "document_id", "values": ["f_1c6ef238fd6ff9297c668f", "f_26a02e42c9e7f21316a70b", "f_31ed814d11c3a9803e2add", "f_61930af0b9a3e482cc61f8", "f_76d02dbb568aaebcebc9bf", "f_922ce9188c3c44bb196668", "f_9bfb378fd5ef606dc48105", "f_e67581da34a3034c7c5e07"]}, "matches": [{"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gdocs/data.json", "pointer": "/docs_documents/67", "field": "document_id", "value": "f_1c6ef238fd6ff9297c668f", "record": {"body_text": "Streak Tutorial Additions\nWe need a couple of new events for the new streak tutorial.\nThe first time a 5 streak is made in a given level\nThe first time a 6 streak is made in a given level\nMinigame Tutorial Additions\nhttps://harmonygamesgroup.Slack.com/archives/C0553V44CE4/p1708019072777519\nWe need to make the tutorial resemble this one.\nWhat we\u2019re missing:\nThe ability to highlight the first tile in the mini-game, as well as the tile on the deck.\nThe ability to display a tutorial element in the post-game screen.\nThe ability to create text bubbles with a button and trigger on the button click.\nThe ability to highlight the matches counter in mini game.\n3. 2nd text bubble\nWe need the text bubble with the tail to use for sophie\u2019s speeches as well as the ability in the tutorial editor to choose between the styles.\nhttps://www.Figma.com/file/mGrkYISQdVRBj52ioFwYzA/Domino-Art-Style-Guide-Version-1.0?type=design&node-id=1471-9&mode=design&t=pucB7JQokFrd8Re4-0\nIt\u2019s in this Figma board above to the very left.\n4. Tailed bubble in the editor\nScene Types\nIt would be great if we could have a scene type called \u201clevel\u201d. And the events will trigger in the number of levels we type in below.\nEvent Triggers\nEvent We Already Have\nButtonClick\nSceneLoad\nObjectClick\nTutorialButtonClick\nTileMatch\nNoMatchAvailable\nDrawFromHandPile\n[USERNAME_46877]\nAnyClick\nDelay\nEvents We Need\nNoTilesLeftInPile:  Basically an event where the player runs out of tiles for the very first time. I want to use it for the +3 booster. But if you can think of a different way to do it, I\u2019m okay with that.\nThe UI Elements That Need To Be Tagged\nThe menu icons, only minigame priority.\nThe models we use to enter each minigame.\nWhere character stands.\nThe boosters on the circular menu, priority wildcard.\nThe streak bar\nThe +3 card\nAdvanced Tiles\nI need a way to point to an advanced tile first time they appear. (Mega, vanishing, and ice) In any way you see fit.", "created_time": "2024-01-02T16:56:22Z", "document_id": "f_1c6ef238fd6ff9297c668f", "drive_file_id": "f_1c6ef238fd6ff9297c668f", "modified_time": "2024-04-18T14:46:41Z", "owner_email": "julia.lawson@harmonygames.co", "revision_id": "a96be0c888", "shared_with_emails": ["arthur.blake@harmonygames.co"], "style_runs": [{"end": 25, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 0}, {"end": 136, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 86}, {"end": 187, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 137}, {"end": 215, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 188}, {"end": 449, "list_id": "list_3", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 359}, {"end": 516, "list_id": "list_3", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 450}, {"end": 598, "list_id": "list_3", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 517}, {"end": 657, "list_id": "list_3", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 599}, {"end": 1056, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1045}, {"end": 1205, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1191}, {"end": 1617, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1579}, {"end": 1657, "list_id": "list_4", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1618}, {"end": 1699, "list_id": "list_5", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1658}, {"end": 1723, "list_id": "list_6", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1700}, {"end": 1777, "list_id": "list_7", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1724}, {"end": 1792, "list_id": "list_8", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1778}, {"end": 1804, "list_id": "list_9", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1793}, {"end": 1819, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1805}], "title": "FTUE Wishlist", "visibility": "domain"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gdocs/data.json", "pointer": "/docs_documents/87", "field": "document_id", "value": "f_26a02e42c9e7f21316a70b", "record": {"body_text": "General Rule Chart\n| Mechanic | Rewind? | Source | Gray Out? |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Core Loop | Yes | [PERSON_NAME_0550] | No |\n| Special Tiles | No | [PERSON_NAME_0550] | Yes |\n| Boosters | No | [PERSON_NAME_0550] | Yes |\n| Character Skills | Yes | [PERSON_NAME_0550] | Yes |\n| Tutorials | Yes | Tutorial Editor | No (Hide UI) |\n| Objectives | Yes | [PERSON_NAME_0550] | No |\n| Streaks | Yes | [PERSON_NAME_0550] | No |\n| Tokens | Yes | [PERSON_NAME_0550] | No |\nCore Loop\nCore Loop means the very basics of the game, meaning matching and drawing. The core loop is rewindable. Mega tile counts within the core loop.\nSpecial Tiles\nSpecial Tiles are the advanced mechanics in the game that change the properties of normal tiles. Vanishing tiles, bomb tiles, etc are examples of special tiles.\nWhen the player interacts with a special tile, the rewind button will go gray and players cannot interact with rewind until they return to the core mechanic.\nException! The vanishing tile will go to its previous color if rewinded.\nBoosters\n\nCurrently, we have 3 boosters in the game.\nBomb: Turns a random normal tile into a bomb tile.\n+3 Cards: Allows players to add 3 more cards to their deck.\nWildcard: Turns a deck tile into a golden tile that allows any match.\n! Rewind exception: A wildcard is not rewindable if it\u2019s acquired as a booster. However, if it comes from a character skill or streak reward, it will be rewindable and the tile will return to deck as intended.\nCharacter Skills\nEach character has special abilities and we call these character skills.\nCharacters have passive skills that activate before a level starts. Therefore, rewind will start grayed out, and after the core loop starts with a match or draw, the rewind button will be usable.\nTutorials\nRewind will be hidden from the board for the duration of any tutorial.\nObjectives\nLevel objectives are displayed in the pre-level dialogue as well as within the game. Players must complete these objectives to earn 2 or 3 stars.\nWe have 4 types of objectives\nLongstreak: Everytime player makes a match the counter goes up.\nCards Left: Player must complete the level with the predetermined number of cards.\nvanishing: Players must match vanishing tiles to complete a level with more starts.\nBomb: Players must use bomb tiles to complete a level with more stars.\nEach of these elements use a dynamic UI. When rewind is used, this UI will need to increase and decrease in number where applicable.\nStreaks\nWhen player uses a rewind, the current streak status will go down one step. If the move that needs to be rewinded is a streak compilation, the reward will be returned.\nTokens\nTokens will be rewindable. If the player has more than 1 token the counter will go down one number. If they have one number the token will simply disappear. The character tile that provided the token will be returned to the board as usual.\nWhat will happen to the character token tile???\nRewind UI and Gold Rule\nRewind will be rewarded to players throughout the game. If they have unused rewinds, the UI will display the number of rewinds available to the player. If the player is out of rewinds, the rewind price will be listed instead and the players may buy rewind at any time with their in-game gold.", "created_time": "2024-04-26T14:19:24Z", "document_id": "f_26a02e42c9e7f21316a70b", "drive_file_id": "f_26a02e42c9e7f21316a70b", "modified_time": "2024-04-29T09:44:40Z", "owner_email": "julia.lawson@harmonygames.co", "revision_id": "f829bfc42d", "shared_with_emails": ["PERSON_2218_EMAIL"], "style_runs": [], "title": "Rewind Spec", "visibility": "private"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gdocs/data.json", "pointer": "/docs_documents/122", "field": "document_id", "value": "f_31ed814d11c3a9803e2add", "record": {"body_text": "Train Level Design Guidelines\nPrefab Selection\nThere are some things to consider when selecting prefabs for optimal train movement and player engagement.\nMake sure the prefab tile count isn\u2019t too much. The levels are more fun when the train is constantly moving. So even when hardcode allows for fast solving keep the prefab pieces to 3-5 range.\nIf you want to use a prefab with more tiles make sure it\u2019s vertically melting away both by layout design and hardcode.\nAlthough horizontal pieces have their place and are fun within the train levels, use them to pace the level. Remember, every time you use a horizontal piece, you\u2019re essentially stopping the train and making the player focus anywhere from 3-5 seconds. Use it wisely and when necessary. Using them as breaks or obstacles is acceptable if it\u2019s not overdone.\n2. Camera Considerations\nFor camera considerations, use the markers effectively, and take advantage of the [PERSON_NAME_0550]\u2019s marker logic. The goal is to show the player the upcoming pieces, so they have a sense of progression and know what more is coming. We never want the train to jerk off and move suddenly. The feeling we give to players should be that they are constantly matching away to unlock the train\u2019s way.\nBe careful about face-up tiles\nTo avoid bugs and cheating, make sure your face-up tiles do not reveal themselves half way. There is no right or wrong way to do it but I find placing a marker a bit below than the prefab does the trick. Make sure you playtest the level until you\u2019re completely happy with the marker placement.\nObserve the marker and open tile border in these screenshots .\nDon\u2019t use too frequent markers\nPlacing the markers too frequently leads to excessive camera movement which it\u2019s motion sickness triggering. If they are too close to each other, even matching the tiles in a horizontal cluster can move the camera 3 times.\nThen observe the in game implications here. \n\n(the branch is broken right now so I couldn\u2019t add screenshots. Go to [PERSON_NAME_0550]\u2019s latest branch \u2018[USERNAME_17813] and observe the last two levels in Chapter 1)", "created_time": "2024-08-09T14:04:36Z", "document_id": "f_31ed814d11c3a9803e2add", "drive_file_id": "f_31ed814d11c3a9803e2add", "modified_time": "2024-08-11T09:36:19Z", "owner_email": "julia.lawson@harmonygames.co", "revision_id": "b147b82df2", "shared_with_emails": ["vincent.parker@harmonygames.co", "brian.foster@harmonygames.co"], "style_runs": [{"end": 46, "list_id": "list_1", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 30}, {"end": 345, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 154}, {"end": 464, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 346}, {"end": 819, "list_id": "list_2", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 465}, {"end": 1272, "list_id": "list_3", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1242}, {"end": 1660, "list_id": "list_3", "list_nesting": 1, "named_style": "NORMAL_TEXT", "start": 1630}], "title": "Train Level Design Guidelines", "visibility": "domain"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gdocs/data.json", "pointer": "/docs_documents/237", "field": "document_id", "value": "f_61930af0b9a3e482cc61f8", "record": {"body_text": "", "created_time": "2024-02-05T17:12:31Z", "document_id": "f_61930af0b9a3e482cc61f8", "drive_file_id": "f_61930af0b9a3e482cc61f8", "modified_time": "2024-02-05T17:12:56Z", "owner_email": "julia.lawson@harmonygames.co", "revision_id": "30209cebd6", "shared_with_emails": [], "style_runs": [], "title": "UI Wish List For Tutorial Iterations", "visibility": "private"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gdocs/data.json", "pointer": "/docs_documents/287", "field": "document_id", "value": "f_76d02dbb568aaebcebc9bf", "record": {"body_text": "[USERNAME_46255]", "created_time": "2023-07-20T18:26:30Z", "document_id": "f_76d02dbb568aaebcebc9bf", "drive_file_id": "f_76d02dbb568aaebcebc9bf", "modified_time": "2023-07-20T19:01:42Z", "owner_email": "julia.lawson@harmonygames.co", "revision_id": "c02f28ff4b", "shared_with_emails": [], "style_runs": [], "title": "MiniGame Idea #1", "visibility": "private"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gdocs/data.json", "pointer": "/docs_documents/364", "field": "document_id", "value": "f_922ce9188c3c44bb196668", "record": {"body_text": "", "created_time": "2025-04-21T11:31:57Z", "document_id": "f_922ce9188c3c44bb196668", "drive_file_id": "f_922ce9188c3c44bb196668", "modified_time": "2025-04-21T12:26:20Z", "owner_email": "julia.lawson@harmonygames.co", "revision_id": "9e12c8cef6", "shared_with_emails": [], "style_runs": [], "title": "Untitled document", "visibility": "private"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gdocs/data.json", "pointer": "/docs_documents/398", "field": "document_id", "value": "f_9bfb378fd5ef606dc48105", "record": {"body_text": "", "created_time": "2024-03-06T16:59:15Z", "document_id": "f_9bfb378fd5ef606dc48105", "drive_file_id": "f_9bfb378fd5ef606dc48105", "modified_time": "2024-03-06T23:06:21Z", "owner_email": "julia.lawson@harmonygames.co", "revision_id": "48f2c5c980", "shared_with_emails": [], "style_runs": [], "title": "UI Implementation List", "visibility": "private"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gdocs/data.json", "pointer": "/docs_documents/574", "field": "document_id", "value": "f_e67581da34a3034c7c5e07", "record": {"body_text": "Nov 24, 2025 | Daily Standup\nAttendees: Marcus Bennett Oliver Brooks [PERSON_NAME_0754] Claire Morgan [PERSON_NAME_9942] [PERSON_NAME_0174] [PERSON_NAME_28884] [PERSON_NAME_0999] [PERSON_NAME_0357]\nNotes\nAction items", "created_time": "2025-11-24T18:45:28Z", "document_id": "f_e67581da34a3034c7c5e07", "drive_file_id": "f_e67581da34a3034c7c5e07", "modified_time": "2025-11-24T18:45:28Z", "owner_email": "julia.lawson@harmonygames.co", "revision_id": "61ac9f61c4", "shared_with_emails": [], "style_runs": [{"end": 28, "list_id": null, "list_nesting": 0, "named_style": "HEADING_2", "start": 0}], "title": "Notes - Daily Standup", "visibility": "private"}}], "records_checked": 633, "files_selected": 1, "files_completed": 1, "scan_complete": true, "errors": []}}, "files_read_this_call": 3, "sources": [{"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/gdocs/data.json", "manifest_sha256": "01005ffefe422717f27a5c3f7820c426dc7a3f15b30fa2c959bbb2acaab1dd2d", "freshness": "55ea7b8ba40ec0fdca868d3538a91844b79ea64f0e4dc0c053af849cadcef3cc"}], "scan_complete": true, "persona_filtered": false, "backend": "grouped-record-scan", "scope_note": "Exact direct fields in selected arrays. No SQL is applied. Absence/uniqueness is supported only within complete declared scopes. Manifest hashes are declared provenance, not fresh full-content hashes."}, "checksum": "ff0bbbe22893b1ef53f81e73e6c0e3bece90ea158f3f25417c7f094f8c83893d"}